@startuml
title Text and image layers: add a title, edit it, see it, export it

actor User
participant "Library (Text tab)" as Library
participant TimelineView
participant TimelineEditor
participant PropertiesViewModel
participant "BuildScene" as Scene
participant ILayerRasterizer
participant ISceneRenderer

alt click a title style (or "Add text")
  User -> Library : click
  Library -> TimelineEditor : AddText(active track, playhead, preset)
else drag a title style
  User -> TimelineView : drop on the timeline
  TimelineView -> TimelineEditor : AddText(track under the pointer, drop time, preset)
end
TimelineEditor -> TimelineEditor : that track if it has room, else a video track\nthat does, else a new one: one undo step
TimelineEditor -> TimelineEditor : select the new clip
TimelineEditor --> TimelineView : TimelineChanged
TimelineView --> User : a text bar (T icon, its own colour)
TimelineEditor --> PropertiesViewModel : selection changed
PropertiesViewModel --> User : tabs for the facets every selected item shares\n(Text, Picture, Position, Fades, Effects)

User -> PropertiesViewModel : change a value (text, font, opacity, X…)
PropertiesViewModel -> TimelineEditor : EditTargets(selected clips, facet)
PropertiesViewModel -> TimelineEditor : SetClipValue(targets, property, value)
note right: every selected clip with the facet,\none undo step; a slider drag coalesces

== every frame (preview and export) ==
Scene -> Scene : for each clip active at t on a video track
alt ILayerClip (text, image)
  Scene -> ILayerRasterizer : Rasterize(clip, w, h, t)
  ILayerRasterizer --> Scene : premultiplied BGRA frame (cached)
  note right: an animated image picks its frame\nfor t, looping (LayerImage.FrameAt)
else VideoClip
  Scene -> Scene : decode the frame
end
Scene --> ISceneRenderer : RenderSource(Frame, HasAlpha, effects, crop)
ISceneRenderer --> User : layer drawn "over" what is below it
@enduml
